  "sharedModel": [
    "Keep CSS box paint in its density/destination map, SVG content in a fitted viewBox/box-inset map, and the natural image boundary independent of both. Never cancel a viewBox transform to recover box coordinates.",
    "Resolve padding on the CSS 1/64 layout grid. All four percentages use the rounded natural image container width. Logical dimensions, SVG percentage bases and text coordinates stay unchanged.",
    "SVGRootPainter projects document content through the snapped outer CSS box. The CSS content clip snaps separately before density; preparation and rendering share the same content map.",
    "Canvas rectangle AA combines with image-boundary coverage before one solid-color store, independently of source opacity and visibility. Packed constant-shader coverage gives different alpha/RGB at fractional edges. Retain the background box independently of SVG content.",
    "Analytic image/content rectangle clips keep independent AA coverage even when geometrically coincident; only their integer enclosure intersects geometrically. They borrow coverage without an output-sized mask. Their scopes restore without requiring an owned reservation; source/filter capture bounds retain their own stages.",
    "Retain one optional declaration source per specified style, rather than per-edge fields throughout retained text. Matching/root tokens use the existing budgeted string owner; resolved scene metadata owns no strings."
  ],
